    "text": "A linearly polarised electromagnetic wave in vacuum is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is incident normally on a perfectly reflecting wall at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>. Choose the correct option.",
